Problem 2. Explain, in your own words, the concept of inheritance.

Inheritance is about reusing and extending a class when making a new one.
A subclass automatically gets the fields and methods of its superclass, but makes it possible to
change or add new methods and fields. It develops an "Is-a" relationship where the subclass "is a..."
"A car is a vehiclge"
"A sock is a clothing"

It shortens code by reusing, and makes a subclass to a subclass to a subclass readable.
